{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>From the midst of the overthrow, in overthrowing the cities.</b> Since he was delivered on Abraham's merit from the midst of the overthrow — while the blessed El was overturning the cities before Lot had yet departed from the entire plain — he would not have merited this in any way had he not fled before the onset of the punishment, yet he tarried, as it says: <b>וַיִּתְמַהְמָהּ</b>. Therefore he feared to dwell in Zoar, for he thought that the overthrow would wait even for Zoar until he himself would be delivered from it on Abraham's merit, and that after his departure from there the overthrow would spread to Zoar as well."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:51.557953563Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}